# Backend

## Module layout

Feature code lives under `backend/src/modules/<name>/`:

```text
modules/<name>/
  <name>.module.ts
  <name>.controller.ts      # HTTP + Swagger only
  dao/                     # Prisma access
  dto/                     # Swagger DTOs + typed exceptions
  use-cases/               # Business orchestration
  *-api.client.ts / *Provider.ts / *-oauth.utils.ts  # infra adapters
```

Existing modules: `health`, `user`, `clerk`, `shopify`, `claude`. Wire new features as Nest modules imported from `AppModule`.

## Dependency injection

- Prefer concrete `@Injectable()` classes registered in the module `providers` array.
- Controllers inject **use cases**, not DAOs or SDK clients.
- Use cases inject DAOs and infrastructure providers.
- Export only what other modules need (e.g. `ClaudeModule` exports `AnalyzeProductUseCase`; `UserModule` exports `UserDao` / `CreateUserUseCase`).
- `PrismaModule` is `@Global()` — do not re-provide Prisma unless mirroring an existing test/health setup.
- There is no generic Nest `*Service` layer; do not add one.

## Use cases

```typescript
@Injectable()
export class GetShopUseCase {
  constructor(private readonly shopifyDao: ShopifyDao) {}
  async execute(email: string) { /* ... */ }
}
```

- One public `execute(...)` entry point.
- Throw Nest HTTP exceptions (`BadRequestException`, `NotFoundException`, typed `*Exception` classes).

## Error handling

- Prefer Nest built-ins for generic failures.
- Domain not-found errors use typed exceptions + Swagger DTOs with a `code` field (e.g. `USER_NOT_FOUND`, `SHOP_NOT_FOUND` in `dto/`).
- Controllers document errors with `@ApiNotFoundResponse`, `refs(...)`, etc.
- Map upstream Shopify/Anthropic failures to gateway/bad-request exceptions; do not leak raw SDK payloads.

## Validation & API

- Global `StandardSchemaValidationPipe` in `main.ts`; Zod schemas may also be parsed in controllers (`safeParse`).
- Shared request schemas: `@recallio/shared/schemas`.
- Routes under global prefix `/api`. Document with `@nestjs/swagger`.
- Auth: `ClerkAuthGuard` on protected routes. Shopify OAuth `callback` stays public. Clerk webhooks use `verifyWebhook`.

## Integrations

### Shopify (`modules/shopify`)

- OAuth: `BeginShopifyAuthUseCase` / `CompleteShopifyAuthUseCase`.
- Tokens: encrypt via `ShopifyOAuthUtils.encryptToken` before DAO writes; obtain plaintext only via `GetValidShopifyAccessTokenUseCase` (server-side).
- Admin API: `ShopifyApiClient` + `createShopifyGraphqlClient` — GraphQL in use cases, not controllers.
- Never return access/refresh tokens to the client.

### Anthropic / Claude (`modules/claude`)

- `ClaudeClientProvider` owns `@anthropic-ai/sdk` client construction from `env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`.
- `ClaudeMessageProvider` wraps `messages.create`.
- Feature use cases (e.g. `AnalyzeProductUseCase`) call the message provider — do not call Anthropic from Shopify controllers/DAOs.

### Clerk

- `clerkMiddleware` in `main.ts`; `ClerkAuthGuard` loads `req.user`.
- User provisioning: `POST /api/webhooks/clerk` → `CreateUserUseCase` / `UserDao`.

## Testing

- Vitest (`backend/vitest.config.ts`). Run: `bun run backend:test` (loads `.env.test`).
- Unit: construct use case with `vi.fn()` mocks (see `test/shopify-auth.security.spec.ts`).
- E2E: `Test.createTestingModule`, override `ClerkAuthGuard`, `supertest`, real `PrismaService` against test DB (see `test/shopify.e2e-spec.ts`).
- Prefer testing use-case security invariants and HTTP contracts over SDK internals.
